WEBVTT

00:10.320 --> 00:12.170
I overslept.

00:12.660 --> 00:15.750
We finally have a magic class...

00:18.450 --> 00:21.120
And I think I slept through it.

00:32.410 --> 00:33.640
As you're a mage,

00:36.240 --> 00:39.000
would you please teach me magic?

02:12.580 --> 02:13.910
Rian?

02:15.190 --> 02:16.510
Tory-san.

02:16.510 --> 02:18.810
Hey, it's Chise.

02:19.300 --> 02:21.460
Have you gotten used to school yet?

02:21.460 --> 02:23.340
Yes, I'm managing.

02:24.800 --> 02:28.650
Um, I'd like to see Elias.

02:28.650 --> 02:30.740
Do you know which room he's in?

02:33.240 --> 02:35.030
I saw Mr. Ainsworth earlier.

02:37.720 --> 02:40.210
He was getting dragged away.

02:42.310 --> 02:43.630
Are you acquainted?

02:44.160 --> 02:45.240
Yes.

02:45.240 --> 02:49.650
He's my... teacher.

02:49.650 --> 02:50.940
Teacher?

02:51.780 --> 02:53.780
Just like us.

02:54.100 --> 02:58.660
Though, I'm more his guardian 
than I am his teacher.

02:59.550 --> 03:00.530
I'm his apprentice.

03:01.860 --> 03:03.040
I see.

03:03.040 --> 03:04.450
That's why you asked about magic—

03:04.450 --> 03:05.300
They...

03:06.390 --> 03:08.670
They went this way.

03:08.670 --> 03:09.750
I'll take you to them.

03:16.180 --> 03:17.400
Thanks.

03:17.400 --> 03:20.050
But weren't you here to see Tory-san?

03:20.320 --> 03:21.940
Only to wake him up.

03:22.560 --> 03:24.340
Chise, Alice.

03:25.570 --> 03:27.850
Be good to him, will you?

03:28.320 --> 03:30.860
I think you guys would be quite compatible.

03:30.860 --> 03:31.950
Right.

03:46.490 --> 03:49.150
So you're Alice Swayne, huh?

03:49.150 --> 03:49.960
Huh?

03:49.960 --> 03:53.330
I've heard rumors about your familiar.

03:54.250 --> 03:57.770
There's no telling how a rumor spreads.

03:57.770 --> 03:59.600
Rumors are scary.

04:00.350 --> 04:02.500
So, Swayne...

04:04.420 --> 04:08.540
You also have the foundations 
needed to use magic.

04:08.540 --> 04:10.770
I'd like to observe, if you don't mind.

04:11.100 --> 04:12.100
Sure.

04:12.100 --> 04:15.930
I have no intention of 
becoming a mage, though.

04:15.930 --> 04:19.130
I'm becoming my master's bodyguard.

04:21.240 --> 04:24.500
This kid isn't cut out to be a mage.

04:24.500 --> 04:25.920
You're right.

04:28.200 --> 04:32.740
She's not one to go along with the rules.

04:32.740 --> 04:36.010
Mages are, you could say...

04:36.350 --> 04:40.500
They're the dimwits who 
get caught up in rules.

04:41.420 --> 04:42.690
Rules...

04:44.560 --> 04:45.550
Hey!

04:47.380 --> 04:48.420
Damn it.

04:48.420 --> 04:49.600
What's wrong with you?

04:51.000 --> 04:53.440
I couldn't help myself.

04:57.060 --> 04:58.360
A fairy?

05:01.170 --> 05:03.310
You're no good.

05:03.310 --> 05:06.320
Your strength smells of rust.

05:07.610 --> 05:09.000
I see.

05:09.000 --> 05:10.110
That's unfortunate.

05:11.540 --> 05:13.720
Why do you want to use magic?

05:16.760 --> 05:19.330
There's someone I want to make happy.

05:22.600 --> 05:25.210
Your job is to protect the students!

05:27.010 --> 05:30.100
From now on, you will make 
safety your <i>top</i> priority!

05:30.430 --> 05:32.080
I got it.

05:32.080 --> 05:34.090
Please stop shouting.

05:35.880 --> 05:38.770
I've never seen Renfred so furious.

05:39.840 --> 05:42.510
Narcisse, why are you here?

05:42.510 --> 05:45.900
You were so intense, I had to spectate.

05:46.410 --> 05:49.730
Besides, I'm not the only 
one in the audience.

05:50.160 --> 05:50.830
See?

05:53.820 --> 05:54.590
Chise.

05:54.590 --> 05:55.630
Alice.

05:58.330 --> 05:59.490
Master!

05:59.990 --> 06:02.000
Do you feel any different 
after using magic?

06:02.000 --> 06:03.320
Elias.

06:02.000 --> 06:03.980
I'm hungry as hell.

06:03.320 --> 06:06.420
That was more exhausting 
than when you scold me.

06:03.980 --> 06:07.630
Ah, the same reaction as 
when you used sorcery.

06:06.420 --> 06:07.630
There, there.

06:11.210 --> 06:13.330
U-Um... Can I help you?

06:14.050 --> 06:17.760
I wasn't sure what to expect.

06:20.780 --> 06:23.850
But hey, you're just a normal girl.

06:24.360 --> 06:26.580
Welcome to the College.

06:26.580 --> 06:31.320
If you're interested in the language arts, 
you're always free to talk to me.

06:33.280 --> 06:35.200
Thank you.

06:36.590 --> 06:39.550
I look forward to working with 
you, too, my new colleague.

06:40.470 --> 06:41.520
Likewise.

06:50.010 --> 06:51.420
Goodness, it's late.

06:51.790 --> 06:54.770
My skin needs plenty of beauty rest!

06:54.770 --> 06:55.890
Good night!

06:55.890 --> 06:56.680
Already?!

06:57.140 --> 07:00.760
Oh, you two, there, have you 
been to the cafeteria, yet?

07:00.760 --> 07:03.400
It's nothing fancy, but there's 
plenty to eat and lots of variety.

07:03.400 --> 07:05.150
Gotta stay well-fed.

07:05.150 --> 07:06.790
The cafeteria...

07:06.790 --> 07:08.210
I'll show you around.

07:08.720 --> 07:09.830
Thanks.

07:11.540 --> 07:12.890
What about you two, Alice?

07:12.890 --> 07:15.340
We'll eat at home.

07:15.340 --> 07:17.200
We haven't been back in a while.

07:19.000 --> 07:20.160
What?

07:20.160 --> 07:23.740
It's just that I've heard you have a habit
 of letting your fists talk for you.

07:23.740 --> 07:24.540
Huh?!

07:24.540 --> 07:26.510
Did you do it again?

07:26.700 --> 07:29.020
I mean, yeah, but I didn't lose!

07:29.020 --> 07:29.910
So you did...

07:29.260 --> 07:31.750
It's <i>their</i> fault for talking behind my back!

07:39.030 --> 07:40.460
Gregory?

07:41.430 --> 07:43.280
How is that new kid?

07:43.280 --> 07:44.390
She's normal.

07:44.390 --> 07:46.440
No different from the other students.

07:46.440 --> 07:48.820
She's not the kind of person who

07:48.820 --> 07:52.710
would be a detriment to the College— 
or rather, to our principal.

07:55.790 --> 07:57.090
Are you happy now?

08:00.570 --> 08:03.280
Inform me if you notice anything unusual.

08:03.280 --> 08:05.780
She isn't the only oddball this year.

08:05.780 --> 08:08.580
We must maintain the balance of power.

08:14.550 --> 08:18.120
The vice principal never gets a break, huh?

08:23.750 --> 08:25.340
This is the cafeteria.

08:25.980 --> 08:29.350
They serve food from 6 AM to 10 PM.

08:29.780 --> 08:32.870
Drinks are self-serve, 24 hours a day.

08:33.320 --> 08:37.000
You can take whatever you want, 
and as much as you want.

08:37.820 --> 08:40.260
There aren't really any 
seating rules, but—

08:40.260 --> 08:41.740
Mr. Ainsworth!

08:42.030 --> 08:45.410
There's so much I want to ask you.

08:45.410 --> 08:47.200
R-Really, now?

08:48.870 --> 08:51.220
You're Chise, aren't you?

08:51.220 --> 08:53.740
We were just eating together.

08:53.740 --> 08:54.800
Wanna join us?

08:55.240 --> 08:57.010
S-Sure. I'd like that.

08:57.470 --> 08:59.990
Well, we'll be waiting over there.

09:06.710 --> 09:09.770
We haven't done our 
introductions yet, have we?

09:10.240 --> 09:12.340
I'm Beatrice Byrne.

09:12.340 --> 09:13.940
Sofia Healey.

09:14.480 --> 09:15.930
Isaac Farrar.

09:16.340 --> 09:18.020
Kevin Forbes.

09:18.020 --> 09:19.570
Martin Chandler.

09:19.880 --> 09:21.710
Jasmine St. George.

09:21.710 --> 09:23.720
Violet St. George.

09:23.720 --> 09:25.810
We're twins.

09:26.250 --> 09:27.530
Um...

09:27.530 --> 09:29.570
Violet's male, right?

09:29.570 --> 09:31.060
Bingo!

09:31.460 --> 09:32.260
Huh?

09:32.260 --> 09:33.840
How could she tell, though?

09:34.340 --> 09:36.590
<i>My dragon's sense of smell
 is surprisingly strong.</i>

09:37.510 --> 09:39.330
Lazarus McGovern.

09:39.330 --> 09:40.860
Roy Truman.

09:41.360 --> 09:44.210
Lastly, I'm Zoe Ivy.

09:44.210 --> 09:46.490
I just started this year, too.

09:46.840 --> 09:48.130
Nice to meet you.

09:48.130 --> 09:49.270
Nice to meet you.

09:50.900 --> 09:52.730
Nice to meet the rest of you, too.

09:52.730 --> 09:53.870
Nice to meet you.

09:55.070 --> 09:56.260
This is mine.

09:56.260 --> 09:57.850
No, man, I brought this here.

09:57.850 --> 09:59.280
It's mine!

09:59.980 --> 10:01.310
Would you like one?

10:01.750 --> 10:03.350
Thank you.

10:03.350 --> 10:04.270
It's mine!

10:04.270 --> 10:05.550
Mine, damn it!

10:05.550 --> 10:07.390
H-Hey, Sofia, I'm just wondering...

10:07.390 --> 10:09.240
Could you pass the pepper?

10:09.240 --> 10:09.910
Oh.

10:10.320 --> 10:11.310
Here.

10:11.310 --> 10:13.080
Why'd <i>you</i> have to get it for me?!

10:13.330 --> 10:16.380
If there's anything you 
want to know, just ask.

10:16.380 --> 10:17.960
Really? Thank—

10:17.960 --> 10:18.520
Dude!

10:18.520 --> 10:19.770
S-Sorry!

10:20.000 --> 10:22.250
Violet, you like these, don't you?

10:22.250 --> 10:23.020
Have them.

10:23.020 --> 10:24.240
Really?

10:24.240 --> 10:25.470
In that case...

10:26.560 --> 10:28.560
Sorry everyone's so noisy.

10:29.250 --> 10:31.740
They all just got here from 
the primary division.

10:31.990 --> 10:33.410
I see.

10:33.800 --> 10:35.620
You're all close, huh?

10:35.420 --> 10:36.100
Is it good?

10:38.930 --> 10:41.570
What's your problem? Why would you say that?

10:41.920 --> 10:42.880
Um...

10:42.880 --> 10:44.210
What about Lucy?

10:44.210 --> 10:45.430
Lucy?

10:45.430 --> 10:46.800
You know her?

10:46.800 --> 10:47.580
Yeah.

10:47.580 --> 10:49.040
She's my roommate.

10:49.410 --> 10:50.530
Huh.

10:52.350 --> 10:54.900
She's always like that.

10:54.900 --> 10:56.220
Don't mind her.

10:56.220 --> 10:57.850
I wonder where the others are—

10:57.850 --> 11:00.120
Oh, speaking of them, there they are.

11:02.510 --> 11:04.460
That's Veronica.

11:04.460 --> 11:07.780
Behind her are April and May Atwood.

11:08.650 --> 11:10.850
And then there's Philomela Sergeant.

11:10.850 --> 11:13.120
Those four are always together.

11:14.510 --> 11:16.910
<i>Her name's Philomela, huh?</i>

11:18.110 --> 11:23.440
So, I heard most mages don't stay 
in one place very long these days.

11:23.440 --> 11:24.710
Whereabouts are you?

11:25.900 --> 11:27.200
Out west.

11:27.200 --> 11:28.830
Way in the countryside.

11:28.830 --> 11:30.450
Wow, that's something you never see.

11:30.450 --> 11:32.060
Rian's hitting on someone.

11:32.060 --> 11:33.740
I don't remember hitting on her.

11:34.460 --> 11:35.610
I'm just teasing.

11:35.610 --> 11:36.670
Sir!

11:37.750 --> 11:40.200
Are you going to stop 
using that other form?

11:40.200 --> 11:42.980
What kind of experiment 
made your head like that?

11:44.820 --> 11:46.720
Hey, no fair!

11:46.720 --> 11:49.260
Sir, would you please be my model?

11:50.190 --> 11:51.220
Model?

11:51.220 --> 11:52.950
May I touch your head?

11:52.130 --> 11:53.400
The shape!

11:53.400 --> 11:54.380
Hey!

12:01.070 --> 12:03.710
Zoe? What's wrong?

12:04.960 --> 12:09.200
Oh, nothing, I just haven't had a meal
 with so many people before.

12:09.200 --> 12:10.880
I'm a little nervous, that's all.

12:11.560 --> 12:14.200
I'm done eating, so I'll see you guys later.

12:17.680 --> 12:18.650
Chise.

12:19.150 --> 12:20.270
Are you all right?

12:20.710 --> 12:21.880
I'm fine.

12:23.470 --> 12:25.350
<i>That wasn't malice.</i>

12:26.500 --> 12:27.520
<i>But...</i>

12:32.230 --> 12:35.030
<i>What's the point of becoming friends?</i>

12:35.030 --> 12:37.180
<i>We're all going to be enemies anyway.</i>

12:38.030 --> 12:40.100
<i>I pity them.</i>

12:48.920 --> 12:51.470
What's wrong with those two?

12:54.400 --> 12:57.280
They aren't human.

13:13.190 --> 13:16.080
One hour time difference, so...

13:18.380 --> 13:19.550
Echos.

13:21.480 --> 13:22.590
Lindel?

13:22.590 --> 13:23.680
Lindel!

13:25.830 --> 13:27.140
<i>Adolf.</i>

13:27.480 --> 13:28.810
<i>What is it?</i>

13:28.810 --> 13:32.950
The sun's down. I thought 
you'd be asleep, old man.

13:33.350 --> 13:35.510
<i>Working so late?</i>

13:35.510 --> 13:38.400
<i>You're quite diligent, young man.</i>

13:38.400 --> 13:40.390
<i>Now, did you need something from me?</i>

13:40.720 --> 13:45.190
Elias Ainsworth has become 
an instructor at the College.

13:45.190 --> 13:46.670
<i>Ah, I'm aware.</i>

13:47.100 --> 13:49.710
<i>To think that young boy's 
become an instructor...</i>

13:51.720 --> 13:55.930
And there's something I'd like 
to ask you regarding that.

13:58.460 --> 14:03.610
Has he ever shown an intent to 
harm another in front of you?

14:03.610 --> 14:07.400
If he has, I'd like to hear 
about the circumstances.

14:07.400 --> 14:10.650
<i>That makes it sound like 
he's already done something.</i>

14:10.650 --> 14:11.400
No.

14:11.400 --> 14:13.560
It's just been on my mind.

14:16.330 --> 14:17.760
<i>Very well.</i>

14:18.140 --> 14:25.570
<i>Adolf, do you know why they 
call him Pilum Muralis?</i>

14:42.170 --> 14:44.250
That was a good nap!

14:47.800 --> 14:48.710
What's this?

15:03.260 --> 15:04.510
You're tired?

15:05.120 --> 15:06.830
Bingo.

15:08.660 --> 15:11.340
So much has happened this week.

15:11.340 --> 15:13.730
You haven't been to school 
in over a year and a half.

15:15.420 --> 15:19.410
I talked a lot, went to class, 
had an examination...

15:19.410 --> 15:20.810
I'm a bit worn out.

15:21.330 --> 15:22.550
Is it unbearable?

15:22.550 --> 15:23.510
No.

15:24.230 --> 15:26.780
I've found something I want to do.

15:26.780 --> 15:29.030
It's a lot of work, but I enjoy it.

15:29.030 --> 15:31.380
Even though a few things are bothering me...

15:36.300 --> 15:37.580
What about you?

15:38.910 --> 15:40.740
Extremely tired.

15:42.460 --> 15:45.840
And being at the College, 
there's something...

15:49.230 --> 15:52.530
It's odd, I feel an urge to 
rub what's on my inside.

15:52.530 --> 15:54.150
An odd sensation.

15:54.150 --> 15:56.890
Elias-isms are pretty obscure.

16:00.160 --> 16:01.550
What's the matter?

16:03.250 --> 16:07.650
I figured I'd try lying on 
the ground like you, but...

16:08.460 --> 16:10.810
Is it your horns?

16:10.810 --> 16:11.560
Yeah.

16:14.530 --> 16:17.670
Elias, could you come 
over here for a second?

16:27.320 --> 16:30.720
This might be the first time 
I've lied down facing the sky.

16:48.160 --> 16:49.480
Silver.

16:49.480 --> 16:50.420
What is it?

16:52.610 --> 16:54.150
Pumpkin scissors?

16:55.440 --> 16:56.620
Right.

16:56.620 --> 16:58.160
It's about time.

16:58.160 --> 17:00.380
Shall we go harvest them?

17:06.780 --> 17:08.900
Is it all right if we rest a little longer?

17:18.860 --> 17:21.850
Are these the types we use on Halloween?

17:22.930 --> 17:23.830
Yes.

17:23.830 --> 17:28.640
I believe the immigrants who went
to America first used pumpkins as lanterns.

17:29.780 --> 17:32.910
Until then, turnips were carved instead.

17:32.910 --> 17:33.730
Turnips?

17:36.710 --> 17:40.030
Halloween used to be known 
as the Samhain festival.

17:41.910 --> 17:45.740
The vibrant summer ends, and the 
darkness of the winter takes over.

17:45.740 --> 17:50.320
The gods of winter and the spirits of the 
dead creep in from the other side at night.

17:50.920 --> 17:55.050
They lit Samhain bonfires to invite 
the spirits of good ancestors.

17:57.930 --> 18:01.440
Though the tradition's been 
long gone for quite some time.

18:02.050 --> 18:06.080
Those gods still exist, though, right?

18:07.340 --> 18:10.560
I don't know if it's right 
to call that an existence.

18:12.600 --> 18:21.410
Long, long ago, they must have been 
revered and worshiped for their powers.

18:22.870 --> 18:27.170
But now, they're a mere facet of 
the seasons and of human activities.

18:27.170 --> 18:30.880
All that remains of them in 
this world is a small remnant.

18:31.610 --> 18:38.890
And like bubbles in a river, 
they pass someone by.

18:39.420 --> 18:41.760
Why did that happen to them?

18:42.370 --> 18:43.770
I don't know.

18:44.480 --> 18:51.230
Perhaps the progression of science has given 
humanity fewer reasons to fear the world.

18:52.560 --> 18:53.740
Say...

18:54.790 --> 18:56.790
We've planted some turnips.

18:56.790 --> 18:59.120
They should be ready for harvest 
just around Halloween.

19:00.560 --> 19:03.160
Shall we try making turnip lanterns?

19:04.190 --> 19:07.030
I'll go wash this at the river, then.

19:07.030 --> 19:08.030
Good.

19:08.030 --> 19:10.920
We'll join you as soon as 
we're done harvesting.

19:22.330 --> 19:24.460
I've done it again.

19:29.870 --> 19:31.430
I still can't get used to it.

19:34.850 --> 19:35.870
It hurts, doesn't it?

19:38.360 --> 19:39.660
Joseph.

19:41.150 --> 19:42.430
Morning.

19:42.430 --> 19:43.630
Morning.

19:47.490 --> 19:48.920
Want this?

19:48.920 --> 19:52.330
Would you at least cook it first?

19:52.870 --> 19:56.360
Besides, I don't eat anything, 
nor do I expel anything.

19:56.360 --> 19:58.000
Not much more than water.

19:58.870 --> 19:59.970
I know.

20:01.040 --> 20:01.880
I'm sure you do.

20:06.380 --> 20:10.380
You aren't getting away anymore, 
even if I pulled out that eyeball.

20:18.970 --> 20:21.900
I'll be borrowing it for a little longer.

20:25.830 --> 20:27.990
I'm getting annoyed. I'm going to sleep.

20:29.150 --> 20:30.390
Sleep well.

20:34.200 --> 20:38.330
I still haven't gotten your answer.

20:41.350 --> 20:42.250
Yeah.

20:43.320 --> 20:44.250
Chise.

20:46.750 --> 20:47.650
You have a guest.

20:52.510 --> 20:53.670
Stella.

20:56.320 --> 20:58.060
Chise!

20:58.900 --> 21:00.230
Stella...

21:00.230 --> 21:01.410
Why?

21:02.010 --> 21:03.520
What do you mean, "Why?"

21:03.520 --> 21:06.900
I texted you saying 
I'd come by this weekend!

21:07.880 --> 21:09.370
I forgot...

21:10.580 --> 21:14.100
Yeah, you don't really check 
your phone too often.

21:14.100 --> 21:16.950
And you seem to be pretty busy 
with your secret school.

21:16.950 --> 21:17.740
Sorry.

21:17.740 --> 21:18.870
Really, I am.

21:22.560 --> 21:23.460
What?

21:26.200 --> 21:27.640
U-Uhm...

21:27.960 --> 21:30.540
You two go on home.

21:30.540 --> 21:32.840
I'll wash the rest myself.

21:34.030 --> 21:36.510
Th-Thank you.

21:46.630 --> 21:49.140
<i>Something seems different from that day.</i>

21:49.620 --> 21:51.290
<i>What's changed?</i>

21:51.730 --> 21:53.090
<i>The circumstances?</i>

21:53.090 --> 21:54.190
<i>Or...</i>

21:55.740 --> 21:57.640
Where'd you get that?

21:58.770 --> 22:00.480
Oh, this?

22:00.480 --> 22:03.250
I'm holding on to it for Elias.

22:03.640 --> 22:05.070
Yeah?

22:10.120 --> 22:11.380
Chise?!

22:11.380 --> 22:12.440
Ruth?!

22:12.860 --> 22:15.270
Hey, where'd you guys go?!

22:20.960 --> 22:22.350
Where are we?
